Adds --variable-latency-errors to Memcheck, so that it reports division and
square root on secret values.

This is the core of the patch from https://kyberslash.cr.yp.to/papers.html
(valgrind-varlat-patch-20250805), limited to the Memcheck sources, with two
changes:

- MC_(eq_Error) also compares isLatency, so that a latency report and an
  address report at the same instruction aren't merged into one.
- Scalar floating-point operations only check the low lane of their operands,
  since a secret in an unused lane doesn't affect them.

